(7076779, 1075450, 119419, '<td valign="top">Ansel Adams on the rocks. Wonderful immediacy in its presence and love the contrast between softness of the human and ruggedness of the rocks.</td>', 'Ansel Adams on the rocks. Wonderful immediacy in its presence and love the contrast between softness of the human and ruggedness of the rocks.', '2013-07-25 06:57:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7076792, 1075869, 12611, '<td valign="top">Such a beautiful shot- a mantra to hold on to. The colors are perfect, the softness of the sky gives way to the appearance of much depth in the dirt-clay ground. The color temperatures are fantastic in range from hot to cool. <br/> <br/>You can''t plan that, you have to feel it. I don''t think enough people stared at this long enough. Perhaps if it was covering the length of a museum wall...</td>', 'Such a beautiful shot- a mantra to hold on to. The colors are perfect, the softness of the sky gives way to the appearance of much depth in the dirt-clay ground. The color temperatures are fantastic in range from hot to cool.  You can''t plan that, you have to feel it. I don''t think enough people stared at this long enough. Perhaps if it was covering the length of a museum wall...', '2013-07-25 09:27:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(7076793, 1075898, 12611, '<td valign="top">I had to come back to this. I feel it probably didn''t get proper respect during the challenge because it is a tougher image to crack, one that you have to look at and let seep it, not click through quickly. Even with the fine toothed comb of a jury vote there probably wasn''t enough time. <br/> <br/>I get the feeling of a dark mushroom Samurai riding public transit, with white silk scarf and the maddening feeling that I can almost focus on what is in my peripheral vision, but it eludes me. All this wrapped up in the Sound of Silence lyric- which is the happiest sad song ever. It also made me think, photography takes a slice of time and transforms it visually, but it also forges a truly necessary silence.</td>', 'I had to come back to this. I feel it probably didn''t get proper respect during the challenge because it is a tougher image to crack, one that you have to look at and let seep it, not click through quickly. Even with the fine toothed comb of a jury vote there probably wasn''t enough time.  I get the feeling of a dark mushroom Samurai riding public transit, with white silk scarf and the maddening feeling that I can almost focus on what is in my peripheral vision, but it eludes me. All this wrapped up in the Sound of Silence lyric- which is the happiest sad song ever. It also made me think, photography takes a slice of time and transforms it visually, but it also forges a truly necessary silence.', '2013-07-25 09:45:17.000000', NULL, 0),
